---
title: Crock Pot Christmas Crack
prepTime: 1 hr 5 min
cookTime: 1 hr 30 min
source.name: Justapinch.com
source.url: https://www.justapinch.com/recipes/dessert/dessert-candy/crockpot-christmas-crack.html
tags: Desserts, Slow Cooker
---

Layer the @unsalted peanuts{1%lb}, @salted peanuts{1%lb}, @semi-sweet chocolate chips{12%oz}, 
@milk chocolate chips{12%oz}, and @peanut butter chips{20%oz} in a large #slow cooker{} 
(starting with the peanuts).

Break apart the @white almond bark{2%lb}(or vanilla candy coating) into chunks and place into the slow cooker as the last layer.

Turn the pot on low, cover with the lid, and leave to cook ~{1%hour}.

Remove the lid and stir to combine.

Replace lid and cook another ~{30%minutes}, keeping an eye on it to make sure it doesn't burn.

Stir again. Spoon mixture in small piles onto wax paper or non-stick aluminum foil.

Allow the candy to harden for at least ~{1%hour}. Enjoy!
